From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:32:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] tests: Expect the screen contents in the arrangement view

With KSCREEN_TEST_SCREEN_COLORS naming the colour a full screen window
shows on each screen, the view must show those colours inside the
screens when Show Screen Contents, in its menu, is checked, and not when
it is unchecked; the event loop must not stop for 250 ms or more while
the pictures arrive, and the captures must leave no file open.

With KSCREEN_TEST_UPOWER_MOCK, a python-dbusmock UPower on the system
bus, the option must follow the power source until the person chooses:
checked on mains power, unchecked on battery. Their choice then wins over
the power source, either way.

With KSCREEN_TEST_EXPECT_REFUSAL, a compositor that refuses captures, the
view must say why and keep working.

With KSCREEN_TEST_STEREO_SCREEN, a screen in a side by side 3D mode that
shows red on its left half and blue on its right, the view must show one
eye as wide as the screen: red at 20 % of its width and blue at 70 %,
where both eyes squeezed into its rectangle would show red at both.

They fail here, where the view shows no screen contents.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
